>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The prog. aims to empower SHG members through different type of vocational trainings. As skill upgradation trainings alone have limited impact on livelihood creation among the members, it envisages conduct of livelihood promotion prog. in clusters. Under this program, the members from 10 to 20 SHGs \(5-6 members from each SHG\) received intensive training on specific domain such as tailoring, bamboo craft & clay ceramic pottery, followed by refresher training, backward-forward linkages and handholding & escort supports. As of March 2024, total 330 new beneficiaries covered and supported to establish their enterprises. 108 women have already established their production units & the progress is going on. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Report)
/E (Report)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (GRAMODYOGA VIKAS YOJANA)
/E (GRAMODYOGA VIKAS YOJANA)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Gramodyog Vikas Yojana is a significant initiative aimed at promoting and revitalizing traditional village industries. Under this convergence program, supported by the Khadi and Village Industries Commission \(KVIC\), 60 pottery artisans were selected to receive intensive training to enhance their skills and productivity. The training, conducted over 10 days and organized into three groups, covered various aspects of pottery making, from traditional techniques to modern practices.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (ENTREPRENEURSHIP & SKILL DEVELOPMENT PROG. \(ESDP\) )
/E (ENTREPRENEURSHIP & SKILL DEVELOPMENT PROG. \(ESDP\) )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The program aims equip trainees with essential entrepreneurial skills and domain-specific expertise. Participants received 6 days of EDP training covering market surveys, marketing, credit appraisal, project report preparation, statutory compliances, registration, and soft skills, followed by 24 days of domain-specific training such as mushroom cultivation, millet products, solar technology, and cosmetology. As a result, trainees are now better prepared to start and manage their own businesses.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (FPO- CENTRAL SECTOR SCHEME)
/E (FPO- CENTRAL SECTOR SCHEME)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (With the support of the scheme, the 1500 FPO members from two FPOs \(Kalasidebi FPC & Datree FPC\) received training in modern farming techniques and business management. They successfully established market linkages, resulting in a significant increase in their income and economic stability. The Kalasidebi FPC has established a food processing unit \(Spices manufacturing unit\) and started marketing, similarly the Datree FPC has established a edible oil processing unit and one nursery and started selling. The FPO also initiated several community development projects, further enhancing the quality of life in the region. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
