/T (EXPOSURE VISITS FOR BLBC MEMBERS)
/E (EXPOSURE VISITS FOR BLBC MEMBERS)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The 18 Block Level Bankers Committee \(BLBC\) Members from two blocks were taken on exposure visits to observe SHGs that are successfully implementing income-generating activities. These visits provided an opportunity for the managers to witness firsthand the operational processes, collaboration, and unity among the SHG members. The exposure visits were conducted in the presence of the District Development Manager \(DDM\) from NABARD and the Lead District Manager \(LDM\), ensuring comprehensive insights and impact of SHGs in fostering economic development.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (TRAINING FOR NGO FIELD WORKERS)
/E (TRAINING FOR NGO FIELD WORKERS)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Under this program, more than 34 NGO field level workers participated in two extensive training sessions. These sessions focused on enhancing their skills in process documentation, project evaluation, and project appraisal, equipping them with the necessary knowledge and tools to effectively manage and assess development projects.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (ENTREPRENEURSHIP DEVELOPMENT PROGRAMME \(EDP\))
/E (ENTREPRENEURSHIP DEVELOPMENT PROGRAMME \(EDP\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (During this program, participants undergo 12 days of intensive training, covering various essential aspects of entrepreneurship. These include conducting market surveys, mastering marketing techniques, understanding credit appraisal processes, preparing project reports, ensuring compliance with statutory regulations, navigating registration procedures, developing soft skills, and acquiring knowledge of GST regulations. Additionally, participants are equipped with numerous other soft skills essential for entrepreneurial success.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
